'\" t
.TH PTY_CELL_TEXT 3 2026-10-03 "libptytest 0.1" "libptytest Manual"
.SH NAME
pty_cell_text, pty_cell_attr, pty_cell_fg, pty_cell_bg, pty_cursor \-
inspect one cell of the screen
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <ptytest.h>
.PP
.BI "const char *pty_cell_text(PtySession *" s ", int " row ", int " col );
.BI "int pty_cell_attr(PtySession *" s ", int " row ", int " col );
.BI "int pty_cell_fg(PtySession *" s ", int " row ", int " col );
.BI "int pty_cell_bg(PtySession *" s ", int " row ", int " col );
.BI "int pty_cursor(PtySession *" s ", int *" row ", int *" col );
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Rows and columns count from 0 at the top-left corner.
.PP
.BR pty_cell_text ()
returns the character in the cell as a UTF-8 string.
A blank cell is \(dq\ \(dq.
A wide character (two columns) is reported in its first column; its second
column returns \(dq\(dq.
Combining marks are part of the string of the character they follow, so
\(dqe\(dq followed by U+0301 is one cell holding both.
The pointer is valid until the screen next changes.
.PP
.BR pty_cell_attr ()
returns the attribute bitmask:
.TS
l l.
PTY_ATTR_BOLD	SGR 1
PTY_ATTR_DIM	SGR 2
PTY_ATTR_ITALIC	SGR 3
PTY_ATTR_UNDERLINE	SGR 4, 21, 4:n
PTY_ATTR_BLINK	SGR 5, 6
PTY_ATTR_REVERSE	SGR 7
PTY_ATTR_INVISIBLE	SGR 8
PTY_ATTR_STRIKE	SGR 9
.TE
.PP
.BR pty_cell_fg ()
and
.BR pty_cell_bg ()
return the colour the program selected, in the form it selected it, so a
test can tell SGR 31 from SGR 38;5;1:
.TS
l l.
0	default (PTY_FG_DEFAULT, PTY_BG_DEFAULT)
30\(en37, 90\(en97	foreground SGR value (PTY_FG_RED: 31)
40\(en47, 100\(en107	background SGR value (PTY_BG_BLUE: 44)
PTY_COLOR_IDX(n)	256-colour palette entry n
PTY_COLOR_RGB(r, g, b)	direct colour
.TE
.PP
.B PTY_COLOR_IS_IDX
and
.B PTY_COLOR_IS_RGB
classify a value.
Reverse video is an attribute: the colours are reported unswapped.
A cell erased while a background colour was selected carries that
background (background colour erase), as on xterm.
.PP
.BR pty_cursor ()
stores the cursor position in the non-NULL arguments.
After a character is written in the last column the cursor stays there
until the next character wraps it, as on a real terminal.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Out of range,
.BR pty_cell_text ()
returns \(dq\(dq and the other cell functions return 0.
.BR pty_cursor ()
returns 1 if the cursor is visible, 0 if the program hid it
.RB ( "CSI ? 25 l" ),
and \-1 for a NULL session.
.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
ASSERT_CELL_TEXT(s, 0, 0, "┌");
ASSERT_CELL_ATTR_EQ(s, 3, 2, PTY_ATTR_REVERSE | PTY_ATTR_BOLD);
ASSERT_CELL_FG(s, 3, 2, PTY_COLOR_IDX(208));
ASSERT_CELL_BG(s, 0, 0, PTY_BG_BLUE);
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pty_row_text (3),
.BR pty_screen_compare (3),
.BR pty_assert (3),
.BR libptytest (7)
